From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Mark the assertion-only locals of row_group_collection.cpp as used

row_group_collection.cpp declares locals that only D_ASSERT() reads (base_row_id),
so in a release build, where D_ASSERT() expands to nothing, they are unused
and -Wunused-variable or -Wunused-but-set-variable says so. Each is cast
to void after its declaration, which changes no behavior.

Carried here until upstream takes it; not proposed upstream yet.

---
diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/storage/table/row_group_collection.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/storage/table/row_group_collection.cpp
--- a/src/duckdb/src/storage/table/row_group_collection.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/storage/table/row_group_collection.cpp
@@ -221,6 +221,7 @@ void RowGroupCollection::Initialize(PersistentCollectionData &data) {
 	stats.InitializeEmpty(types);
 	auto l = owned_row_groups->Lock();
 	auto base_row_id = owned_row_groups->GetBaseRowId();
+	(void)base_row_id;
 	for (auto &row_group_data : data.row_group_data) {
 		D_ASSERT(row_group_data.start == base_row_id + total_rows.load());
 		auto row_group = make_uniq<RowGroup>(*this, row_group_data);
